<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="040" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Plugin package and spaarke-decisions skill</title>
    <phase>D Registration, deploy and live E2E</phase>
    <gate>after 003 and 030</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Creates new manifest, skill and script files with explicit constraints; no .cs/.ts code</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Package authoring against documented schemas (app manifest 1.30, agentConnectors) with the April package as a layout reference</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>G</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/** and its CI step; 022 touches none</parallel-reason>
    <deps>003, 030</deps>
    <tags>config, ci-cd, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Create the Copilot/Cowork plugin package at src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/ (app manifest 1.30 with agentConnectors pointing at the BFF's /mcp/legal-operations per environment) with the spaarke-decisions skill, and a build gate that enforces skill names ^spaarke(-[a-z0-9]+)+$ at 64 characters or fewer.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in Microsoft 365 app manifests, Copilot plugin packages and Cowork skills.</role>
  <goal>The package builds to a zip with a valid 1.30 manifest, slug spaarke and explicit display name 'Spaarke'; the spaarke-decisions skill tells Copilot when to call spaarke_show_decisions using the approved terms; the name gate runs in CI and rejects bad names.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-16; design §5; naming note §1 (plugin slug spaarke, display 'Spaarke'; skill spaarke-decisions; gate agreed with legal-ai-accelerator-r1, OD-20). Plan decision: folder src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/; this task may move it if the build tooling requires, recording the change in notes/decisions.md. Phase 0 T2 (plugin package rendering) informs the manifest.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/appPackage/manifest.json (1.30, agentConnectors, env placeholders)</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/appPackage/color.png and outline.png (copied from src/solutions/CopilotAgent/appPackage/)</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/skills/spaarke-decisions/SKILL.md</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/scripts/validate-plugin.mjs (name gate + manifest checks)</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/package.json (build zip; test runs the gate)</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/client-tests.yml (run the package's npm test)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/solutions/CopilotAgent/appPackage/ (April package layout, env.dev.json placeholders)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/coordination/2026-11-06-copilot-naming-and-ownership.md §1</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">T2 and T14 results (package behaviour, display name)</dependency>
      <dependency task="030" status="pending">client-tests.yml edited first (file ownership)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Names exactly per the naming note: package slug spaarke with explicit display name 'Spaarke'; skill folder and name spaarke-decisions; connector display 'Spaarke'; never 'Spaarke Copilot' or 'Spaarke Connect'.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">validate-plugin.mjs fails on any skill name not matching ^spaarke(-[a-z0-9]+)+$ or longer than 64 characters, and on a manifestVersion other than 1.30; it runs in CI through client-tests.yml.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The skill text uses 'Work Item' and 'Decision Record'; uses 'Finding' only for billing link-outs (D-208); qualifies 'playbook' by format where the format matters (D-209); never instructs the model to complete a decision (O-14).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The manifest holds no secret, tenant id or client secret; environment values (BFF URL, app ids) are placeholders resolved per environment, as env.dev.json does for the April package.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/declarative-agent/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>knowledge/m365-copilot</file>
      <file>knowledge/declarative-agents</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/coordination/2026-11-06-copilot-naming-and-ownership.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/phase0-results.md</file>
      <file>src/solutions/CopilotAgent/appPackage/manifest.json</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read T2/T14 results and the April package layout.</step>
    <step order="2">Write manifest.json (manifestVersion 1.30, explicit name 'Spaarke', agentConnectors to {bffBaseUrl}/mcp/legal-operations) and copy the icons.</step>
    <step order="3">Write skills/spaarke-decisions/SKILL.md: when to call spaarke_show_decisions (direct prompts about decisions waiting on the user in Spaarke), what the widget does, the approved terms, and what not to do.</step>
    <step order="4">Write validate-plugin.mjs and fixture tests for the gate; wire npm test and the zip build; add the step to client-tests.yml.</step>
    <step order="5">Build the zip locally and validate the manifest against the 1.30 schema.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If manifest 1.30 rejects agentConnectors in this shape, or the build tooling needs another folder, STOP, record the evidence and the proposed path in notes/decisions.md, and ask the owner before moving it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Phase 0 showed skills cannot reference connector tools (T10), STOP and escalate before writing the skill.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The April package src/solutions/CopilotAgent/appPackage (a declarative agent with an OpenAPI action, not agentConnectors).</existing>
    <extension>No: it is a different package type and manifest version (1.30 agentConnectors), and FR-17 alone may rebuild the April package.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Cowork has no / entry point and no documented widget route for Spaarke, so FR-16's /spaarke-decisions acceptance fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Install (npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund), build and test TypeScript projects</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/</output>
    <output type="test">src/solutions/CopilotPlugins/spaarke/scripts/validate-plugin.mjs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The package builds to a zip; manifest.json validates against the app manifest 1.30 schema with an agentConnectors entry pointing at the /mcp/legal-operations placeholder URL.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The package slug is spaarke and the display name is explicitly 'Spaarke'; the skill folder and name are spaarke-decisions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the gate rejects 'Spaarke-decisions', 'spaarke_decisions', 'decisions', 'spaarke-' and a 65-character name, and accepts 'spaarke-decisions' (fixture tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the gate rejects a manifest whose manifestVersion is not 1.30.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The skill text uses 'Work Item' and 'Decision Record', uses 'Finding' only for billing link-outs, never says 'Spaarke Copilot' or 'Spaarke Connect', and never tells the model to complete a decision (grep evidence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No secret or tenant id is in any package file (grep evidence); client-tests.yml runs the gate.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Deployment of the package to the dev tenant (upload and admin approval) is part of 042, run by the owner.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
